//! expect-check-fail: a value parameter is a pointer to one complete record or scalar; this is not one (§16.2b.5)
//! expect-check-fail: = help: a pointer with a count is 'buffer param P len param L'; text is 'text param P'; an opaque record is a resource ('resource Name wraps *mut T')
// D198 / D244 (§16.2b.5): a value-parameter clause names a pointer to one
// complete flat record or scalar — never `void *`.
use c_import("static inline int ignore_ptr(const void *n) { return n != 0; }")

c contract shapes:
    fn ignore_ptr
        reads param n

fn main:
    print("unreachable")
